---
/* ============================================================
   PullQuote — a line lifted out of the body copy.

     <PullQuote>Falling is just never fun.</PullQuote>

   A centred statement block in the reading measure, banded by a heavy
   rule above and a hairline below.

   It deliberately does NOT hang in the margin. A true margin pull
   quote has to sit BESIDE a paragraph, and in this grid each block is
   its own row — so a hanging quote ends up alone on a line with a void
   next to it, which reads as a bug rather than as typography. Centred
   in the measure is unambiguous and looks intentional at every width.

   Pull quotes REPEAT text that already appears in the body — they are
   decorative emphasis, so the element is aria-hidden to stop screen
   readers reading the sentence twice.
   ============================================================ */
---

<div class="pull" aria-hidden="true">
  <p><slot /></p>
</div>

<style>
  .pull {
    margin: var(--space-12) 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .pull p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    line-height: 1.28;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
    /* a touch narrower than the measure so it reads as a lifted line,
       not as another paragraph */
    max-width: 32ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-6) 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
